%% Drel release flow sequence: gates, recorded approval, publish surfaces, rollback
%% Source of truth: docs/diagrams/release-flow.mmd
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant D as Maintainer
    participant E as Evidence archive<br/>docs/testing/results/
    participant G as GitHub main + CI
    participant W as CF Worker<br/>api.drel.app
    participant T as TestFlight
    participant U as Acceptor (you)
    participant P as CF Pages site
    participant S as Self-hosted server

    rect rgb(245,247,251)
    Note over D,E: 1. Gates and evidence (both pass and fail are archived)
    D->>D: bump project.yml version+build<br/>CHANGELOG entry with Scope/Verified/Evidence
    D->>D: verify-release-notes / identity<br/>docs-links / repo-hygiene / release-gate
    alt a gate fails
        D->>E: the failure report is archived too
        D->>D: fix, then start over
    else all green
        D->>E: release-drel.sh tag then test<br/>report + recording + evidence archived
    end
    end

    rect rgb(253,245,230)
    Note over D,U: 2. Acceptance (the release decision is yours)
    E-->>U: test report + TestFlight build
    U->>U: accept on a real device<br/>push, sound, lock screen
    alt rejected
        U-->>D: send back (evidence stays, no rerun)
        D->>D: fix, tag and test again
    else accepted
        U-->>E: confirm --approved-by "you"<br/>the approver is written into the report
        Note over E: without a recorded approval<br/>publish refuses to run
    end
    end

    rect rgb(238,243,255)
    Note over D,S: 3. Publishing (one automatic surface, three manual)
    D->>G: git push main
    G->>G: CI gates: conventions, release purity,<br/>design lint, smoke tests
    alt drel-api-proxy changed
        G->>W: automatic wrangler deploy
    end
    D->>T: publish the TestFlight build (manual)
    D->>P: local preview accepted, then publish (manual)
    D->>S: bump ServerVersion, rsync, restart,<br/>verify /health (manual)
    D->>G: push tag v(ver)+(build)
    end

    rect rgb(255,240,240)
    Note over D,S: 4. Rollback (every layer has a path)
    D->>W: wrangler rollback<br/>(code rolls back, DO data does not)
    D->>T: disable the broken build,<br/>previous builds stay installable
    D->>P: Pages instant rollback
    D->>S: restore the previous binary / conf backup
    end
